{"annotation_id": "L33-R01", "dataset_line": 33, "chunk_id": "chunk_900ff38ca0d01eeabbb4f2518baef2e6fcfc8f06a2e68ee094491523462f4ee1", "source_url": "https://fastapi.tiangolo.com/tutorial/metadata/", "content_hash": "chunk_f478d7b9dc5cc29d8458a8b7883545941ff69f39ca77fe6af1ff4686d4aa29d8", "annotation_status": "pending_review", "notes": "The opening sentence scopes the fields in the table to API metadata.", "kind": "relationship", "source": "license_info", "relation_type": "PART_OF", "target": "API metadata", "evidence": "## Metadata for API\n\nYou can set the following fields that are used in the OpenAPI specification and the automatic API docs UIs:\n\n| Parameter | Type | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `title` | `str` | The title of the API. |\n| `summary` | `str` | A short summary of the API. Available since OpenAPI 3.1.0, FastAPI 0.99.0. |\n| `description` | `str` | A short description of the API. It can use Markdown. |\n| `version` | `str` | The version of the API. This is the version of your own application, not of OpenAPI. For example `2.5.0`. |\n| `terms_of_service` | `str` | A URL to the Terms of Service for the API. If provided, this has to be a URL. |\n| `contact` | `dict` | The contact information for the exposed API. It can contain several fields. `contact` fields | Parameter | Type | Description | | --- | --- | --- | | `name` | `str` | The identifying name of the contact person/organization. | | `url` | `str` | The URL pointing to the contact information. MUST be in the format of a URL. | | `email` | `str` | The email address of the contact person/organization. MUST be in the format of an email address. | |\n| `license_info` | `dict`", "support": "explicit", "proposed_relation": null, "raw_candidate_ids": [], "post_validation_candidate_ids": [], "cause": "not_extracted", "cause_status": "pending_review"}
